From 83485e811b6ecc5d06e209a10df47c0961cd2997 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: claude <claude@example.com>
Date: Wed, 27 May 2026 18:11:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: make custom widget send flow actually work

- Require widgetId from URL and fail loud if missing, rather than self-declaring
  ready after 5s. Element substitutes $matrix_widget_id into the widget URL
  template; without it the WidgetApi transport drops every inbound message and
  the widget appears connected but is not.

- Drop StickerpickerCapabilities, MatrixCapabilities.Screenshots, and the
  sendSticker / raw postMessage fallbacks. Element only grants m.sticker to
  widgets whose state event has type 'm.stickerpicker', so requesting it from a
  custom widget pollutes the approval prompt for nothing and the sendSticker
  call is always rejected.

- Request only m.send.event:m.image and m.send.event:m.room.message, the
  capabilities a custom widget can actually receive. Element prompts the user
  to approve them.

- Add a NotifyCapabilities handler so Element stops logging 'The postMessage
  was unhandled' for capability negotiation. Register all handlers before
  start() so we don't miss Element's opening messages.

- sendGifAsImage now throws SendGifError on failure instead of returning a
  boolean. The UI was previously displaying a preview-cleared 'success' state
  for sends that silently failed; it now surfaces the real error.

- Document the required URL template placeholders ($matrix_widget_id,
  $matrix_user_id, $matrix_room_id, $theme) in the README, and the capability
  approval prompt the user must accept.

Refs: #2
