@@ -122,14 +122,21 @@ GIPHY_API_KEY=your-giphy-key
 
 ### Widget URL Examples
 
+> **Important:** when adding the widget through Element (or any client that uses
+> the [matrix-widget-api](https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-widget-api)
+> templating), the URL **must** contain the placeholders below. Element
+> substitutes them at load time. Without them, the widget has no
+> `widgetId` and the Widget API transport will silently drop every inbound
+> message, leaving the widget stuck on "Connecting…".
+
 Production (proxy, no key in URL):
 ```
-https://gif.your-domain.com/?provider=tenor
+https://gif.your-domain.com/?provider=tenor&widgetId=$matrix_widget_id&userId=$matrix_user_id&roomId=$matrix_room_id&theme=$theme
 ```
 
 Development (direct API):
 ```
-http://localhost:5173/?provider=tenor&apiKey=YOUR_KEY
+http://localhost:5173/?provider=tenor&apiKey=YOUR_KEY&widgetId=$matrix_widget_id&userId=$matrix_user_id&roomId=$matrix_room_id&theme=$theme
 ```
 
 ## Adding Widget to a Matrix Room
@@ -137,8 +144,14 @@ http://localhost:5173/?provider=tenor&apiKey=YOUR_KEY
 ### Element Web
 
 1. Open a room
-2. Click the room name → **Settings** → **Integrations**
-3. Add a custom widget with your deployed widget URL
+2. Click the room name → **Settings** → **Extensions** (or **Integrations** in
+   older builds)
+3. **Add custom**, paste the templated URL above (with all `$matrix_*`
+   placeholders intact — do not pre-substitute them), and submit
+4. **Approve the capability prompt** that appears inside the widget area:
+   "Allow this widget to send messages on your behalf" with `m.image` and
+   `m.room.message`. If you don't see this prompt, the widget cannot send
+   anything; remove and re-add the widget.
 
 ### Via Matrix State Event
 
@@ -149,12 +162,23 @@ http://localhost:5173/?provider=tenor&apiKey=YOUR_KEY
   "content": {
     "type": "im.vector.modular.widgets",
     "name": "GIF Picker",
-    "url": "https://gif.your-domain.com/?provider=tenor",
+    "url": "https://gif.your-domain.com/?provider=tenor&widgetId=$matrix_widget_id&userId=$matrix_user_id&roomId=$matrix_room_id&theme=$theme",
     "data": {}
   }
 }
 ```
 
+### Capabilities
+
+The widget requests these Widget API capabilities at startup:
+
+- `m.send.event:m.image` — required to send the GIF as an `m.image` message
+- `m.send.event:m.room.message` — same, broader matcher some clients require
+
+Element will prompt the user to approve them. The widget does **not** request
+`m.sticker` or `StickerpickerCapabilities`, since those are only granted to
+widgets whose state event has `type: "m.stickerpicker"`.
+
 ## Tech Stack
 
 - **Backend**: Express 5 (serves SPA + proxies GIF APIs)
